-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       The Official Father Christmas Game
  Publisher   Alternative Software, 1989
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Official Father Christmas Game, The (1989)(Alternative).z80
  MD5         71dd57b2ece2787dfff915bf3ba50d3f

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: level 1's figures in their own white on a double-buffered
              Layer 2, in the game's own plot order, over the original bitmap;
              their plots and restores at 28 MHz; the overlay off at room
              builds and text screens

  Note        Keys: on the menu 1 keyboard, 2 Sinclair, 3 Kempston; on the
              name wheel O and P turn it, Space picks, ED. ends it. In play P
              right, O left, Q up, A down, Space fire. The original look with
              the clash gone in level 1, the house: Santa and the elves keep
              their white at the table, the stool and the ladders, where they
              used to take the cell's colour; the scenery keeps its own. Their
              ink is drawn on Layer 2, in the game's order, over the original
              bitmap. Levels 2 (white on black) and 3 (the sky's bands, by
              design) are as the original. Fits a 1MB Next. Known issues: pace
              in JNext -0.15% to -0.09% over whole runs, slowest 20 updates
              +0.67%. Santa's top rows can lag a frame at the table and
              ladders. Missing: an Enhanced colour set; natural play to the
              end; hardware untested.

