-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Run by script through the real loader on a NextZXOS 26.11 card
              copy; 1.0 not yet played by the owner; published at his request

  Replay      3 scripted recordings (menu, name wheel, level 1 walking,
              ladders, elves; one with test pokes into levels 2 and 3): 37472
              frames, 46281 hooks run original and build from one state each:
              every register including R and all 48K RAM, stack too:
              IDENTICAL; 11265 Layer 2 pictures, 5538961 pixels, against an
              independent model and against the ULA bitmap: IDENTICAL; 10
              broken builds caught; 640 ABI cases, each hook entered at all 4
              CPU speeds, both IFF values, 8 R phases; the start-up exact with
              and without NEXLOAD

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: through the real .NEXCLASH loader on a
              private NextZXOS 26.11 card copy, output byte for byte as nxc.py
              makes it, reaching play; 15-minute soak against the original;
              flicker check clean

  Coverage    Scripted input, no human play: level 1's first rooms, ladders,
              elves, room changes; levels 2 and 3 by a test poke. Not reached:
              natural completion, level 1's later rooms

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
